__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db
*.bak
debian/.debhelper/
debian/ele-messenger/
debian/debhelper-build-stamp
debian/files
debian/*.substvars

# Node-local runtime config. This repo is PUBLIC and config.json names this
# machine's tailnet and LAN addresses. Only eleadmin.py reads them, purely to
# display, and load_config() already returns {} when the file is absent -- so
# a fresh clone works without it. Copy config.example.json and fill it in.
config.json

# Flutter build OUTPUT. pkg-client/usr/ held the compiled desktop client --
# including libapp.so with the server hostname baked in at compile time, which
# --replace-text cannot rewrite because it skips binaries. Build artifacts do
# not belong in a public repo; build them from flutter/ instead. The packaging
# metadata (DEBIAN/control, PKGBUILD) stays tracked.
pkg-client/usr/
flutter/build/
/target
